    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43248" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑτέρ-ωθεν</span></b>  (or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕτερ-θε</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Hes.
			<u>Sc.</u>
			281
		</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
			A.D.
			<u>Adv.</u>
			194.4
		</span></i>), Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>from the other side</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.247
			</span></i>, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ δ᾽ ἑτέρωθεν</span>
			v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				22.91
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in pregnant
			sense with Verbs of rest, <i>on the other side, opposite</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕστηκ</span>' <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				3.230
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				6.247
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>from another quarter, from outside</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				17.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				702c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1121a34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Bato
				5.9
			</span></i>.</div>
